  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  name: pykmclib\n  version: \"0.0.1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/LiuGaoyong/pykmclib/releases/download/v${{ version }}/${{ name }}-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 9a5650b0f3e16e7825eac8b7cee54c6ca9abf7e8e2c1a9ed6c6702d0349e3aa9\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  script:\n    - if: unix\n      then: export CMAKE_GENERATOR=Ninja\n    - ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - if: build_platform != target_platform\n      then:\n        - python\n        - cross-python_${{ target_platform }}\n        - pybind11\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - cmake >=3.21\n    - if: unix\n      then: ninja\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - scikit-build-core >=1.1\n    - pybind11 >=3.0\n  run:\n    - python\n    - numpy >=1.21\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - pykmclib\n        - pykmclib.Backend\n      pip_check: true\n  - script:\n      - python -c \"from pykmclib.Backend import Backend, Custom; assert Backend.MPICommons.isMaster()\"\n      - pytest -q tests\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - pytest\n    files:\n      source:\n        - tests/\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/LiuGaoyong/pykmclib\n  summary: Lattice kinetic Monte Carlo simulations (Python front end, C++ backend)\n  description: |\n    pykmclib repackages KMCLib, the general framework for lattice kinetic Monte\n    Carlo simulations, as a modern Python distribution built with\n    scikit-build-core and pybind11. The computationally heavy backend is the\n    original KMCLib C++ code; the Python API follows upstream KMCLib.\n  license: GPL-3.0-or-later\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - third_party/KMCLib/LICENSE.txt\n  documentation: https://github.com/LiuGaoyong/pykmclib\n  repository: https://github.com/LiuGaoyong/pykmclib\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - LiuGaoyong\n",
